 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abcc5b71-338b-577c-85eb-afb6840553f8" :answer/id #uuid "abcc5b71-338b-577c-85eb-afb6840553f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b948344f-4402-5976-9213-69a3217d38b4" :answer/id #uuid "b948344f-4402-5976-9213-69a3217d38b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-947b312e-ee99-59a7-af09-a903fd2e1d0c" :answer/id #uuid "947b312e-ee99-59a7-af09-a903fd2e1d0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad0f1713-2b05-514d-a10e-779d012891f3" :answer/id #uuid "ad0f1713-2b05-514d-a10e-779d012891f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8739b76-a0ab-5c98-9470-0410c9781bfe" :answer/id #uuid "f8739b76-a0ab-5c98-9470-0410c9781bfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4439689-3a8b-5ab4-811b-957340569ef9" :question/id #uuid "b4439689-3a8b-5ab4-811b-957340569ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-96838" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{11,13,14,16,20\\},$ compute $P(13\\le X<16).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{11,13,14,16,20\\},$ and the set $S=\\{11,13,14,16,20\\}$ has $|S|=5$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}, & x=11,13,14,16,20 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(13,14)$ that satisfies $13\\le X<16.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(13\\le X<16)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-562db703-36ec-5628-89c0-8362fc1a8c9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-562db703-36ec-5628-89c0-8362fc1a8c9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "562db703-36ec-5628-89c0-8362fc1a8c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bf21e23b-1364-514e-b8af-73c89ab25898" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9875fe05-05a7-53d3-ada2-9e8fce9c093c" "answer-cd6aedae-2775-57fe-a720-4bb794b417b9" "answer-8959248e-670f-5708-9f80-641e8f900f4f" "answer-bf21e23b-1364-514e-b8af-73c89ab25898" "answer-7bf42ba7-f2a3-55cc-af79-9f295ed44f49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9875fe05-05a7-53d3-ada2-9e8fce9c093c" :answer/id #uuid "9875fe05-05a7-53d3-ada2-9e8fce9c093c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd6aedae-2775-57fe-a720-4bb794b417b9" :answer/id #uuid "cd6aedae-2775-57fe-a720-4bb794b417b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8959248e-670f-5708-9f80-641e8f900f4f" :answer/id #uuid "8959248e-670f-5708-9f80-641e8f900f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf21e23b-1364-514e-b8af-73c89ab25898" :answer/id #uuid "bf21e23b-1364-514e-b8af-73c89ab25898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bf42ba7-f2a3-55cc-af79-9f295ed44f49" :answer/id #uuid "7bf42ba7-f2a3-55cc-af79-9f295ed44f49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a7e41369-c44a-5b84-b7fc-e764205aba15" :question/id #uuid "a7e41369-c44a-5b84-b7fc-e764205aba15" :question/math-academy-id "q-96839" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{1,2,3,…,17\\},$ compute $P(2\\le X<9).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{1,2,3,…,17\\},$ and the set $S=\\{1,2,3,…,17\\}$ has $|S|=17-1+1=17$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{17}, & x=1,2,3,…,17 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $7$ items $(2,3,4,5,6,7,8)$ that satisfy $2\\le X<9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(2\\le X<9)=7\\cdot \\frac{1}{17}=\\frac{7}{17}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6928beb7-6d1c-5fe0-9c89-497534fd649e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6928beb7-6d1c-5fe0-9c89-497534fd649e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6928beb7-6d1c-5fe0-9c89-497534fd649e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9c17240f-6dc3-5a02-ad81-bc045176e81b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-de19a84f-848b-52ac-9d4f-56ab8e8d674a" "answer-16d2517e-9185-5017-857d-9ebe5b8407f6" "answer-9c17240f-6dc3-5a02-ad81-bc045176e81b" "answer-35e889ba-9472-5ac8-a25c-ed6d2ba99992" "answer-0a450533-8c93-5f65-b086-433237dedd04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de19a84f-848b-52ac-9d4f-56ab8e8d674a" :answer/id #uuid "de19a84f-848b-52ac-9d4f-56ab8e8d674a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16d2517e-9185-5017-857d-9ebe5b8407f6" :answer/id #uuid "16d2517e-9185-5017-857d-9ebe5b8407f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c17240f-6dc3-5a02-ad81-bc045176e81b" :answer/id #uuid "9c17240f-6dc3-5a02-ad81-bc045176e81b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35e889ba-9472-5ac8-a25c-ed6d2ba99992" :answer/id #uuid "35e889ba-9472-5ac8-a25c-ed6d2ba99992" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a450533-8c93-5f65-b086-433237dedd04" :answer/id #uuid "0a450533-8c93-5f65-b086-433237dedd04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163251 :tutorial/content "A discrete random variable $X$ follows a **discrete uniform distribution** over a set $S$ if each value in $S$ is equally likely. \n\nThe probability mass function for the discrete uniform distribution on a set $S$ is given by\n\n![](images/61/61fd8cf495b429392260fbad1b671c9c48c8f681827653aaabe73a4dbf6b6ecf.svg)\n\nWhen a random variable $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over the set $S=\\{ s_1, s_2, \\ldots, s_n\\},$ we denote it as\n\n$$\nX \\sim U \\left\\{ s_1, s_2, \\ldots, s_n\\right\\}\n$$\n\nand we say that $X$ is **uniformly distributed** over $S.$\n\nFor example, consider the random variable $T\\sim U\\{1,2,4\\}.$ In this case, $S = \\{1,2,4\\},$ $|S| = 3,$ and therefore the probability mass function for $T$ is\n\n![](images/d1/d19075d50e24a2fc9d157311535d0665103b1498ef99312606c4cf6c482cfe1a.svg)\n\nA sketch of $f(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/cb/cbac12f164635cd4efaa94167a4582689d470c3373769e1aa9facc2670f732ef.png)\n\n**Note:** In this lesson, we will make use of the following formula for computing the cardinality of a set of consecutive numbers:\n\n$$\n\\left| \\{ a, a+1, a+2, \\ldots, b \\} \\right| = b - a + 1\n$$\n\nDon't forget about the $+1$ at the end of the formula. The $+1$ is needed because we are including both endpoints $a$ and $b$ in the count. (Not convinced? Notice that $\\left| \\{ 4, 5 \\} \\right| = 5 - 4 + 1 = 2.$)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162167 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
